      "reason": "Candidate 14 passes as supplied. Hole 1 is a dry 405-yard narrow-corridor par 4. The straight corridor and fairway bunkers make placement matter, while 8 of 9 tee-dispersion samples remain playable. Hole 2 is a 576-yard uphill par 5 with a substantial lake to the right of play. Its broad landing area supports a safer route away from the shoreline, while pressing closer to the water creates a meaningful risk-reward choice; 6 of 9 tee probes are playable. Hole 3 is a dry 142-yard, 7-iron par 3 with bunkers around the target. Its 9 of 9 safe probes make it the scoring opportunity, contrasting with the demanding long hole. The par-4/5/3 sequence, different tee clubs, and change from corridor placement to shoreline management to a short target shot give the round solid internal variety. Recent rounds feature frequent water hazards and longer target carries; limiting water to the par 5 and finishing with a dry short par 3 gives this set sufficient freshness. The challenging par 5 is balanced by recoverable misses on the opener and an accessible but bunkered target finish, so the round is fair without being uniformly easy. Geometry facts confirm water on Hole 2 only. No edits are needed.",
